{
  "dom_id": "step-q135707",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Given that $t\\ge 0,$ simplify $-36t+|-24t|.$",
  "worked_solution": "Firstly, since $|-a|=|a|,$ we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n-36t+|24t|.\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-36t+|24t| & = \\\\ -36t+|24|\\cdot |t| & = \\\\ -36t+24\\cdot |t| & = \\\\ -36t+24|t| & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $t\\ge 0,$ we have that $|t|=t.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-36t+24|t| & = \\\\ -36t+24t & = \\\\ -12t & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
